<title>THAILAND: SCF FINANCE SAYS TO RAISE CAPITAL.</title>
<headline>SCF FINANCE SAYS TO RAISE CAPITAL.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>SCF Finance and Securities Plc plans to issue 435 million shares at 10 baht per share, the firm said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The issue would raise the company's registered capital to five billion baht ($161 million) from 650 million, the firm said.</p>
<p>SCF was one of 42 ailing finance firms suspended by the Bank of Thailand on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The firm said it is also seeking foreign or local partners and will split its finance and securities operations.</p>
<p>A shareholders meeting is set for September 5, the statement said.</p>
<p>($1 = 31 baht)</p>
